'''Death''' occurs when a player's [[Hitpoints]] reach zero; a message in the [[Chat Interface]] will inform them: {{mes|Oh dear, you are dead!}}. Death can also occur when alternative criteria are met{{explain}}, such as being completely frozen at the [[Wintertodt]] which causes the player's death despite not losing any Hitpoints, or reaching a fatal number of Doom stacks within the [[Fortis Colosseum]]. After death, the player will [[respawn]] at another location and potentially deal with further consequences, such as [[Items Kept on Death|losing or breaking some items]].

==Unsafe and safe deaths==
{{See also|Items Kept on Death}}
Deaths are often classified as either unsafe/dangerous or safe. However, these terms depend on the context; deaths can have various consequences depending on the circumstances. Generally:  
* A death is considered unsafe for [[File:Hardcore ironman chat badge.png]] [[Ironman Mode#Hardcore Ironman|Hardcore Ironmen]] if it will result in the loss of their status (or a pooled life in the case of [[File:Hardcore group ironman chat badge.png]] [[Group Ironman Mode#Hardcore Group Ironman|Hardcore Group Ironmen]]), and safe if it doesn't. Some activities that are safe for Hardcore Ironmen are unsafe for Hardcore Group Ironmen.
* A death is considered unsafe for your items if it will result in your items being [[Items Kept on Death#Breakable items|broken]], sent to a [[deathbank]], left on your [[grave]], or dropped to another player; and the death is considered safe for your items if it doesn't affect them.

Deaths in most parts of the game are considered unsafe, while some [[minigames]] or activities allow deaths without extra penalty. For more information on items kept or lost upon death, see [[Items Kept on Death]].

== Death animation ==
===Death overrides===
[[File:Death Animations.png|frame|The Death Animations interface.]]
[[Animation override]]s are available for dying, which can be toggled by speaking to [[Death (NPC)|Death]] in [[Death's Office|his office]] and asking him to change how you die.

The interface allows players to select one or more animations that play out upon death. If multiple are selected, one of the selected animations will be chosen at random.
